e a crappy worker on your team but  unfortunately most Amazon managers  aren't that lucky given that everyone  that they hire for the corporate side  are exceptional if they were to score  their team members the worst performer  might be given a 90  obviously there is some room for  improvement but it's definitely not a  fireable offense managers very much  understand that this would be unfair and  that's why they turned to hiring to fire  they usually maintain a core team of  seven to ten people that they want to  keep permanently and every year they'll  hire some random sucker who will be  tasked with doing all of the dirty work  for the team for a year before getting  fired if a given sucker truly does an  exceptional job there is a chance that  they'll be allowed to stick around but  this means that someone else on the team  now has to be fired insteaded and this  is by design a lot of companies don't  care about tenure or experience in fact  they feel like these attributes make an  employee less productive because they've  become too comfortable these companies  would much rather have a bunch of  short-term employees that work their  butts off the entire time they're there  and this forces managers to either hire  to fire or hire to replace it's truly  quite a vicious practice but it's not  just Amazon who's guilty of this most  old-school corporate Giants practice  some form of this think companies like  GE IBM and even Microsoft up until 2013.  we shouldn't note however that it wasn't  until after 2013 that Microsoft finally  started to grow again so this practice  is definitely just as counterproductive  as it sounds but nonetheless many  companies still practice it leading to  constant over hiring followed by layoffs  and firing  foreign  while it might be easy to say that  companies should just hire what they  need it's usually not that simple the  underlying problem is that the number of  employees that a company needs is simply  not constant Facebook having a hundred  thousand employees in 2021 it might not  have been enough but Facebook having a  hundred thousand employees in 2022 is  definitely Overkill when everyone is  spending and buying it companies that  naturally need more employees conversely  when everyone is pulling back companies  needed less employees combine this with  varying levels of productivity and  opportunities and that this issue just  becomes even more magnified but this  doesn't mean that companies that are  completely innocent either many of them  engage in terrible practices like hiring  to fire or hiring to replace which not  only increases churn but also creates a  horrendous workplace culture which makes  the entire organization less productive  really the only way to avoid this is to  join some sort of background company  like an energy company or a water  company or of course the government but  for the rest of us well we'll probably  have to deal with these corporate games  throughout the rest of our careers but  that's just what I think what are your  thoughts on hiring to fire comment that  down below also drop a like if you're  hoping that the layoffs end sooner  rather than later and of course consider  checking out our Discord Community such  as fertility ideas and to consider  subscribing to see more questions  logically answered but until then I'm  Hari and I'll see you guys on next one


